    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Gen6 application",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Table 'BAC-9301 2-PIPE FCU OBJECTS', pdf pages 46-47 of the guide.",
    "The guide gives no read/write column; access is inferred (inputs read-only, outputs commandable, calculated values and display icons read-only, setpoints and configuration writable).",
    "Descriptions carry the factory default from the guide; multi-state state lists are numbered 1..n in printed order (the printed defaults use that numbering).",
    "Objects depend on controller model and application, and can be deleted or created in KMC Connect, Converge or TotalControl.",
    "Placeholder objects named AV_nn / BV_nn ('Analog Value #nn') are spare objects in the default database."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Conquest Gen6 Controller Application Guide",
